---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Accessibility"
  description="Accessibility features, known limits, and feedback availability for Psychology Blog."
>
  <div class="container narrow section">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Reading should feel open</p><h1>
        Accessibility matters here.
      </h1><p>
        Our aim is a usable, understandable reading experience for as many
        people as possible.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How the site is designed</h2><p>
        The site uses a light theme, familiar system fonts, generous line
        spacing, and readable text sizes. The layout adapts to smaller screens.
        You can zoom the page using your browser's controls.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>A skip link lets keyboard users move to the main content.</li><li>
          Links and controls have visible focus indicators.
        </li><li>
          Articles use headings, key takeaways, and reference links.
        </li><li>Article text links are underlined.</li><li>
          Reduced-motion preferences are respected.
        </li><li>Reading does not require an account.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Our target and current limits</h2><p>
        We aim to meet WCAG 2.2 Level AA. This is a design target, not a
        statement of independently audited conformance. Automated checks cannot
        establish that every person can use a page.
      </p><p>
        A human review with keyboard navigation, screen readers, zoom, and
        different devices is required before public launch. External websites
        and media players may have different accessibility support.
      </p>
      <h2>Audio, video, and transcripts</h2><p>
        Media is disabled at launch until real items are available. When
        enabled, videos load only after you choose to open the player.
        Descriptions are required for media items. The owner must verify
        captions and provide accessible transcripts before treating media as
        ready for publication.
      </p>
      <h2>Tell us about a barrier</h2><p>
        The owner's accessibility contact has not yet been supplied. See <a
          href="/contact/">contact availability</a
        >. When a channel is available, please share the page link, what you
        tried to do, and what happened. Do not include private health
        information.
      </p>
      <p>
        Last updated 6 November 2026. This statement will be reviewed after
        human testing and when features change.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
